{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3336","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3336","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3336\",\"parent_revision\":\"3f398277a9daa985be6491ceb8a5a4b89f5ba65f\",\"root_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe root cause behind #3329's deletion, generalized: `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` re-explained MCP tool parameters and return shapes in hand-written prose that the tool's own docstring/`Field(description=...)` annotations already stated \u2014 and that duplicate was structurally guaranteed to drift, because FastMCP regenerates the live tool schema from the code every server start, while a prose copy in a skill file changes only when someone remembers to edit it. That mechanism is what produced the deleted skill's \\\"12 tools\\\" heading against 28 real ones, a dead storage-format claim, and a broken `fastmcp` invocation example.\\n\\nConfirmed during #3329 this isn't unique to that one skill: `plugins/development-harness/README.md`'s \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical shape (filed separately as #3335).\\n\\nGoal: audit other `dh:*` skills for the same pattern \u2014 prose that restates an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior, checkable live against the tool's actual schema via `ToolSearch`. Where found: delete the restatement from the skill, and if a genuine content gap exists, add it to the tool's own docstring instead (verified in #3329 to be the correct destination \u2014 it's literally the schema the agent is shown when deciding how to call the tool, a stronger and self-maintaining hook that a skill-file restatement can never be).\\n\\nUser-provided context: see #3329 for the full investigation this generalizes from, including three concrete examples where this exact check (comparing a doc's claim against the live `ToolSearch` schema) revealed the doc was either already redundant or actively wrong.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:43:13.508056Z</sub>\\n\\n## Claim 1: artifact_register enum coverage in create-artifact/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation incomplete and contradictory instruction)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file lists only 7 of 10 live `artifact_type` enum values, missing `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report`. Skill also explicitly instructs agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` even though `task-plan` is a valid enum member on the live schema.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Live `artifact_register` schema enum contains 10 values: feature-context, architect, task-plan, T0-baseline, TN-verification, codebase-analysis, code-review, research, dispatch-plan, audit-report\\n- Skill file table (lines 61-68) documents only 7 types: feature-context, codebase-analysis, code-review, architect, T0-baseline, TN-verification, research (omits dispatch-plan, audit-report, and task-plan from table)\\n- Skill file section \\\"task-plan\\\" (lines 128-132) redirects users away from `artifact_register`: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage. Create them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)` and retrieve them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)`\\\" \u2014 contradicting the valid schema enum value\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `artifact_register` enum parameter (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md lines 128-132\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 2: backlog_update milestone parameter in groom-milestone/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation claims unsupported feature)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file (line 89) states `backlog_update(selector, ...)` can \\\"assign milestone,\\\" but live `backlog_update` schema has no `milestone` parameter.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file line 89 lists tool as: \\\"`backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_update` schema parameters: content, description, entry_id, plan, reason, replace_section, section, selector, status, title, verified \u2014 no `milestone` parameter present\\n- Schema is silent on milestone assignment through backlog_update\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_update` parameters (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md line 89\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 3: #-prefixed beads nanoid selector format in implement-feature/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (claim supported through schema pattern inference)\\n\\nclaim: Comment (lines 142-143) states \\\"#\\\"-prefixed beads nanoids fail to resolve as a `selector` parameter: \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file comment (lines 142-143): \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_groom` selector parameter description lists valid formats: \\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)\\\"\\n- Schema separates formats: `#N` (for numbers only) and `beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)` (shown without # prefix)\\n- The schema example `bd-a3f8` (not `#bd-a3f8`) supports the skill's claim that # does not pair with beads nanoids\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_groom` selector parameter description (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 142-143\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T09:48:18.754462Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: chore: Audit other dh:* skills for hand-written MCP tool documentation that duplicates and drifts from live tool schemas\\nDate: 2026-08-30\\nGoal: Find and fix (or file) other dh:* skills that restate MCP tool parameters/return shapes in prose that drifts from the live ToolSearch schema, the same mechanism that caused #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current inventory of dh:* skill directories under plugins/development-harness/skills/ (post-#3329 deletion count) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Which of those skills (SKILL.md + bundled references/agents files) contain prose naming or describing an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. For each candidate hit, whether the live tool schema (via ToolSearch) already states the same thing verbatim/equivalently (REDUNDANT), contradicts it (STALE), or omits it (GAP) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Whether any confirmed GAP is small enough to relocate into the tool's own docstring inline during this task, versus large enough to warrant its own follow-up item | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill) overlap with any candidate found here (they should be excluded, already tracked/closed) | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:38:33.138074Z</sub>\\n\\n**Wave 0 pre-swarm research \u2014 hand-written MCP tool documentation drift in dh:* skills**\\n\\nMethod: enumerated all `plugins/development-harness/skills/*/` directories (63 post-#3329), grepped SKILL.md + `references/*.md` + `agents/*.md` across all of them for MCP tool names (`backlog_view`, `backlog_groom`, `backlog_list_issues`, `backlog_update`, `artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, etc.), filtered bare-invocation mentions (not a drift risk) from prose that names/describes parameters, return fields, or behavior, then compared each candidate hit against the live schema via `ToolSearch(\\\"select:<tool>\\\")` and one live `backlog_view` call.\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md` (STALE + GAP, high confidence)**\\n\\nThis entire skill file exists to restate `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_register`'s parameters and return shape in prose. It has already drifted the same way the deleted `dh:backlog` skill did (#3329):\\n\\n- Lines 56-68, \\\"## Parameters > `artifact_type`\\\" table lists 7 recognized type strings: `feature-context`, `codebase-analysis`, `code-review`, `architect`, `T0-baseline`, `TN-verification`, `research`. The live `artifact_register` schema's `artifact_type` field is an enum of **10** values \u2014 the table omits `task-plan`, `dispatch-plan`, and `audit-report` entirely. `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report` are not mentioned anywhere else in the file either \u2014 silent drift, structurally identical to #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\n- Lines 128-132 go further and are actively **contradictory**: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage\u2026 Create them with `sam_plan`\\\" \u2014 instructing agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` to `artifact_register` \u2014 while the live schema lists `task-plan` as a valid `artifact_type` enum member for that exact tool. Either the tool's enum is stale (still exposes a value the skill says is invalid) or the skill's guidance is stale (the tool now supports it); either way this is a direct, checkable contradiction between skill prose and live schema, not just an omission.\\n- Lines 24-52 (\\\"## Invocation\\\" and the return-value paragraph) restate `item_id`, `artifact_type`, `artifact_id`, `status` (enum `draft|current|superseded|archived`, default `\\\"current\\\"`), `agent` (default `\\\"\\\"`), `content` (required, non-empty), and the return dict shape (`registered`, `artifact_count`, `action` \u2208 {\\\"added\\\",\\\"updated\\\"}, `content_stored`, `messages`, `warnings`). Checked against the live docstring/schema \u2014 this part is REDUNDANT (accurate, near-verbatim duplicate) rather than stale, but it's the same duplication mechanism that produced the `artifact_type` table drift above: hand-copied schema that only updates when someone remembers to.\\n\\nRecommendation: this file is the strongest candidate for the remediation this item calls for \u2014 delete the `artifact_type` table and the Invocation parameter restatement (redundant with live schema), fix or resolve the `task-plan` contradiction (verify current tool behavior first), and keep only what `ToolSearch` cannot provide: the CLI-equivalent invocation, the \\\"when to use this skill vs sam_plan\\\" trigger guidance, and the producing-agent-per-type mapping (arguably a genuine content addition \u2014 recommend relocating into the `artifact_type` enum member descriptions in the tool schema itself rather than the skill, per this item's stated destination-of-record).\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 86-89 (STALE, medium confidence)**\\n\\n\\\"## MCP Tools Used\\\" one-line list:\\n```\\n- `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 load milestone items and groomed status\\n- `backlog_view(selector)` \u2014 read individual item Impact Radius and metadata\\n- `backlog_groom(selector)` \u2014 trigger grooming for ungroomed items\\n- `backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\n```\\n`backlog_update`'s live schema has no `milestone` parameter at all \u2014 its fields are `content`, `description`, `entry_id`, `plan`, `reason`, `replace_section`, `section`, `selector`, `status`, `title`, `verified`. The claim \\\"assign milestone\\\" is not supported by any parameter on this tool as currently schema'd \u2014 either milestone assignment happens through a different, unnamed mechanism, or this line is stale. Needs a fact-checker follow-up to confirm which.\\n\\nLower-confidence secondary note on the same block: `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 the live `milestone` param is typed `string`, described \\\"Filter by milestone title\\\", not a numeric ID; the skill's `N` naming may mislead an agent into passing an integer. `backlog_groom(selector) \u2014 \\\"trigger grooming\\\"` is a loose paraphrase (the live tool is a content-write/sync operation, not an action-trigger) but low-stakes as a one-line tools-used pointer.\\n\\n**CANDIDATE GAP \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 148-155 (unverified, needs fact-check)**\\n\\nInline comment on a `backlog_groom` call: `{issue}` is `str | int`... \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\" The live `backlog_groom`/`backlog_update`/`backlog_view` `selector` field description (\\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid\\\") does not capture this specific nanoid-prefix failure mode. This reads as a genuine operational GAP (real caller-facing behavior the schema omits) rather than redundant restatement \u2014 but it was not independently verified against `find_item`'s source in this pass; recommend Wave 1 fact-checker confirm the claim before treating it as ground truth to relocate into the tool docstring.\\n\\n**CHECKED, NOT AN ISSUE \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md` lines 78-81**\\n\\n\\\"`backlog_view(selector, summary=false)` \u2014 returns full item context including `sections` dict (groomed fields), labels, and priority.\\\" Verified against a live `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3336\\\", summary=False)` call in this session \u2014 the response does include `sections`, `labels`, and `priority` top-level keys. REDUNDANT (accurate today) \u2014 carries the same future-drift risk as any hand-copied schema summary, but not currently wrong. Not a remediation priority.\\n\\n**Overlap check**: neither #3335 (README.md \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table) nor #3329 (deleted `dh:backlog` skill, no longer present in this tree) intersect with any file listed above \u2014 confirmed by directory listing, `dh:backlog` skill directory does not exist post-#3329, and `create-artifact`/`groom-milestone`/`implement-feature`/`dh-meta-docs` are all distinct skills from the README and the deleted skill.\\n\\n**Not exhaustively covered**: `dispatch`, `interop`, `multi-perspective-review`, and the `work-backlog-item` workflow reference tree (60+ files) were grepped for tool-name mentions but most hits there are bare invocation examples (selector/section/content passed through), not parameter/behavior restatement, and were not individually diffed against live schemas at `standard` depth \u2014 a `deep`-depth follow-up pass could extend coverage there if the groomer/RT-ICA assessor judges the three confirmed findings above insufficient to close the item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"827b30e1f152af408aadfbdf53dfb8e64d6675c0f5536060023dedd31b641f26\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRe4n5A\"}"}